    <string name="phone_bg_enter_code">Enter pairing code</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_code_desc">Or type the code here, with Wireless debugging open beside Pinky in split screen.</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_code_dialog_desc">The six-digit code from Pair device with pairing code. Keep that dialog open.</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_code_hint">Six-digit code</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_not_a_code">The code has six digits.</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_wrong_code">That code didn\'t work. Check the code in the dialog and try again.</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_no_dialog">Pinky couldn\'t find the pairing dialog. Open Pair device with pairing code and keep it open while you enter the code.</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_pair_failed">Pairing failed: %1$s</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_paired">Paired. Pinky can use the background screen.</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_pair_channel">Pairing</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_pair_notify_title">Pair Pinky</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_pair_notify_body">In Wireless debugging, tap Pair device with pairing code, then enter the code here.</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_forget">Forget pairing</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_forget_desc">Pinky deletes its key. To remove Pinky from the phone too, tap it under Paired devices in Wireless debugging.</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_forget_confirm">Pinky deletes its pairing key and drops its connection. You\'ll need to pair again to use the background screen.</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_confirm_title">Use Wireless debugging?</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_confirm_body">Wireless debugging gives Pinky the access a computer has when it debugs this phone. Pinky uses it only to run its screen helper, which opens the hidden second screen, starts apps on it, and shows and controls it. It doesn\'t use it to install apps, read your files or change settings. Pinky connects only while this is on and drops the connection when you turn it off.</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_confirm_ok">Turn on</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_safety">What Pinky does with Wireless debugging</string>
    <string name="phone_bg_safety_body">Pinky pairs with this phone only, and keeps its key in its own storage. While the background screen is on, Pinky holds a debugging connection to the phone and uses it only to run its screen helper: it opens the hidden second screen, starts the task\'s apps there, and shows and controls that screen. Approvals and taking over work as on the phone\'s screen. Turn this off and Pinky drops the connection; Forget pairing deletes the key. Android turns Wireless debugging off when the phone leaves Wi-Fi: tasks then run on the phone\'s screen.</string>

